  "landfallEstimate": "To cross south Andhra Pradesh coast as a",
  "rawBulletin": "REGIONAL SPECIALISED METEOROLOGICAL CENTRE -TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 12\nDEMS-RSMC SPECIAL TROPICAL CYCLONES NEW DELHI DATED 02.11.2026\nFROM: RSMC \u2013TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTO: STORM WARNING CENTRE, NAYPYITAW (MYANMAR)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, BANGKOK (THAILAND)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, COLOMBO (SRILANKA)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, DHAKA (BANGLADESH)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, KARACHI (PAKISTAN)\nMETEOROLOGICAL OFFICE, MALE (MALDIVES)\nOMAN METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT,\nMUSCAT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nYEMEN METEOROLOGICAL SERVICES,\nREPUBLIC OF YEMEN (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nNATIONAL CENTRE FOR METEOROLOGY, UAE (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nPRESIDENCY OF METEOROLOGY AND ENVIRONMENT,\nSAUDI ARABIA (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nIRAN METEOROLOGICAL ORGANISATION, (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nQATAR METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 12 FOR NORTH INDIAN OCEAN (THE BAY OF\nBENGAL AND ARABIAN SEA) ISSUED AT 2000 UTC OF 02.11.2026 BASED ON 1800 UTC\nOF 02.11.2026\nSub: - Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu] over Westcentral Bay of Bengal off\nSouth Andhra Pradesh Coast\nThe Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu]\u201d over Westcentral Bay of Bengal off South\nAndhra Pradesh Coast moved north-northwestwards with a speed of 8 kmph during past 6 hrs and lay\ncentered at 1800 UTC of today, the 02nd November, 2026 over the same region near Latitude 15.1\u00b0N and\nLongitude 80.4\u00b0E, about 50 km east-northeast of Kavali (43243, Andhra Pradesh), 50 km southeast of\nOngole (43221, Andhra Pradesh), 90 km north-northeast of Nellore (43245, Andhra Pradesh), and 150 km\nsouth-southwest of Machilipatnam (43185, Andhra Pradesh).\nLandfall process commenced from 1930 UTC. The outer spiral band in the northern sector entered into the\nsouth Coastal Andhra Pradesh. Wall cloud region in the forward sector is approaching towards the\ncoastline.\nIt is very likely to continue to move north-northwestwards and cross south Andhra Pradesh coast as a\nSevere Cyclonic Storm with wind speed of 100 to 110 kmph gusting to 120 kmph between Nellore (Andhra\nPradesh, 43245) and Narsapur (Andhra Pradesh, 43187), close to Ongole (Andhra Pradesh, 43221)\naround 2200 UTC of 2nd November, 2026.\nCloud distribution: (a) Isolated: <25%, Scattered:25-50%, Broken: 51-75%, Solid:>75%, Convection Intensity: (a) Weak: Cloud Top Temperature(CTT)>-\n25\u00b0C, (b) Moderate: CTT:-25\u00b0Cto-40\u00b0C, (c) Intense: CTT: -41\u00b0Cto -70\u00b0C and (d) Very Intense::Less than -70\u00b0C Probability of cyclogenesis (formation of\ndepression) :NIL:0%, LOW:1-33%, MODERATE:34-66% and HIGH:67-100%\nThis is a guidance Bulletin for WMO/ESCAP Panel Member countries. Visit respective National websites for Country specific Bulletins.\nThe Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d is under the continuous surveillance of Doppler Weather Radars at\nChennai, Machilipatnam and Visakhapatnam.\nForecast location and intensity are given in following table:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(UTC) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n02.11.26/1800 15.1/80.4 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/0000 15.5/80.1 90-100 gusting to 110 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/0600 15.9/79.9 70-80 gusting to 90 Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/1200 16.3/79.8 65-75 gusting to 85 Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/1800 16.7/79.8 55-65 gusting to 75 Deep Depression\n04.11.26/0600 17.4/79.9 40-50 gusting to 60 Depression\nThe estimated central pressure is 994.0 hPa and maximum sustained wind speed is 55 kt\ngusting to 65kt.\nNellore reported mean sea level (MSLP) of 1010.3 hPa, 24 hours pressure change (P24) as -1.9\nhPa and maximum sustained wind speed (MSW) as 2700/05kt, Kavali reported MSLP of 1008.1\nhPa, P24 as -4.7 hPa and MSW 3200/12kt, Bapatla reported MSLP of 1010.6 hPa, P24 as -2.0\nhPa and MSW 500/11kt, Ongole reported MSLP of 1008.4 hPa, P24 as -3.7 hPa and MSW\n3600/10kt.\nAs per latest INSAT 3DS imagery based on 1800 UTC, Vortex (Murasu) over west-central bay off\nAndhra Pradesh coast and neighbo",
